/*
 * ============================ NOT BUILT ============================
 * DRAFT ONLY.  This file is intentionally NOT named *.dtsi so that no
 * #include can pick it up by accident, and it is NOT included from
 * tegra194-p3668-0001-p2151-0000.dts.
 *
 * Read build/kernel-E/f2-watchdog-OPTIONAL-NOT-BUILT/README.md before
 * doing anything with it.  Short version: enabling this arms the Tegra
 * watchdog AT PROBE TIME (nvidia,enable-on-init), the final expiry is a
 * system POR (which very likely wipes the ramoops black box), and the
 * first userspace open of /dev/watchdog permanently disables the kernel's
 * own petting IRQ (CONFIG_WATCHDOG_NOWAYOUT=y).
 *
 * Deploy ALONE, on top of an otherwise known-good kernel + DTB, and only
 * after F1 (ramoops) has been proven to work.
 * ===================================================================
 *
 * Tegra WDT0 / TMR7, timeout 120 s, expiry-count 5.
 * Feeder in this configuration = the kernel's own threaded IRQ handler
 * (tegra_wdt_t18x_isr -> __tegra_wdt_t18x_ping).  Do NOT additionally set
 * systemd RuntimeWatchdogSec until this has been stable for days.
 *
 * To use: drop the ".OPTIONAL" suffix and add, as the LAST include in
 * tegra194-p3668-0001-p2151-0000.dts:
 *     #include "tegra194-mi-k91-watchdog.dtsi"
 */

&tegra_wdt {
	status = "okay";
};
